# Surfaces

Do not tune one card. Change placement/ingest so the next email, Offload, and calendar event behave the same way.

## Home

Dated **admin** due today, overdue, or within 7 days: form, RSVP, payment, named errand with a deadline. This-week events with open work (gala + form + kit) are **one** Home card. Cap **5**, order **stable by due day**. Visiting Home must not swap two valid cards. See all is the rest of that same pool — not Radar leftovers.

## Radar

Holds, far-dated admin, and leftover packing grouped under the parent. A this-week cluster already on Home is not also on Radar. Not the Offload inbox.

## Lists

- **Shopping**: groceries only.
- **General to do**: every other chat/manual todo (book the eye test, email the teacher, accommodation).
- **Named lists**: only if the user taps Add a list. Never because an item has children.

## One thing, one card

- Hold = one Radar card. No extra “buy a new X”.
- This-week event with open work (gala + medical form + kit; farm slip + packed lunch) → **one Home card**, parent title, children as the checklist. Not a second form card and a Radar kit group.
- Informational context with no children (INSET, nursery closed) stays off Today's Actions.
- Far RSVP / far admin can stay a standalone Home card. Invented interview prep is not Home.
- “No gifts” → no Present/Card/donation. Party is context; **RSVP** is the action.
- Children of a dismissed/done parent stay off Home and Radar.
- Mixed Offload (“oat milk and email the teacher”) splits: shopping + to-do, never grocery-only.

Typed fields only. `source` is provenance, never a switch. Keep tests in `lib/placement.selftest.ts`, `lib/intake-contract.selftest.ts`, `lib/radar-organize.selftest.ts`, `lib/shopping.selftest.ts`.
